From fd8ddda0d0cef5109e949a9cac6539b9562bce9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 17:14:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.5.5: first-boot credential gate + rmcpd pin
 retention + wait modal + live internet status

Four backlog items on the primary RT-BE96U:

1. Unbypassable first-boot credential gate (CISA AA26-194A hygiene). New themed
   Reaper_FirstBoot.asp forces the admin username+password on a factory-clean box
   (via the proven httpApi.chpass, defpass_enable=0 so the default password is
   disabled). state.js retargets its existing first-run redirects: password-default
   -> Reaper_FirstBoot.asp, and Wi-Fi-unconfigured (sdn_rl==default) -> the proven
   Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp until a PSK is set. Derived from live state so an
   already-configured/upgraded box never sees the gate. reaper_inject.c skips the
   new page (renders standalone).

2. AI Advisor IP pin retained: reaper_mcp.cgi status now returns rmcp_client and the
   Advisor UI prefills the pin field, so it survives visits/reboots and is no longer
   wiped by a later Save Settings.

3. Reusable themed "waiting" modal (reaper_shell.asp: reaperWait/reaperWaitDone),
   wired into Reaper_Advisor apply/arm (Reaper_QoS already had its own overlay).

4. Internet status self-updates during boot: dashboard card + header WAN pill now
   poll wan0_state_t/wan0_ipaddr (appGet.cgi) and flip to Connected on their own
   (fast while down, slow once up).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
